Bootstrap recipes: built before arch/order, for the tools Arch builds
with themselves (cmake needs cmake's own build tools; python-build and
python-installer need each other). A recipe's "# replaces:" line names the
Arch package bases it stands for: build-wave.sh counts them as done.
"sha256 = TODO" is filled in from the downloaded file on first use.

rust is the Rust project's binary release before Arch's version: Rust is
only built with Rust (Arch builds it with its previous rust). It has no
"# replaces:" line, so Arch's rust is still built from source and replaces
it as an upgrade; "bootstrap:<name>" in the done list keeps it from being
built again meanwhile.

go is the same for Go: Arch's go is built with a Go tree in /usr/lib/go
(GOROOT_BOOTSTRAP); the Go project's binary release, older than Arch's,
gives it one, and the go built from source replaces it.

gengetopt is the same for gengetopt: Arch's is built from Git, which has
not the option parser gengetopt generates for itself (makedepends
gengetopt); the GNU release before Arch's version has it generated.
